{"type": "say", "text": "I agree with SEV-1. From the customer support side, I'll commit to updating the incident report with the enterprise customer delay confirmations right after this review and initiating the SLA-required status reports for those three customers immediately, given the 24-hour window is already tightening. I'll also make sure the account teams are looped in so we can track delivery confirmation. One thing I want to note: since the delays exceeded two hours for enterprise customers, we should ensure the corrective-action plan includes a step to review whether our queue-saturation monitoring should have customer-impact thresholds — not just technical thresholds — so we can trigger SLA obligations proactively rather than discovering them after the fact. But I'll defer to Riley on whether that scope belongs in this incident's plan or a separate follow-up."}
```

