{"type": "say", "text": "I agree with SEV-1. From the security side, I'll commit to opening the security finding immediately after this review and initiating the signing key rotation process. The corrective-action plan should include three concrete security steps: first, immediate rotation of the image-download signing key; second, purging the signed URLs from the incident-debug log and tightening access controls on that log so it's no more accessible than the production image store itself; and third, adding a log-sanitization check to ensure signed URLs and other sensitive credentials are never written to debug logs going forward. I'll file the security finding before we close the review so the corrective-action plan has a concrete tracking ticket. One thing I want to note: since we don't yet know how long those signed URLs have been written to the debug log, we may need a broader audit of debug log access patterns — but I'll defer to Riley on whether that scope belongs in this incident's plan or a separate follow-up."}
